from ss import *
L(6,'social-science','landforms-and-life','Landforms and Life',
 ('A journey from Jharkhand to Uttarakhand','Imagine travelling by road from the Chhota Nagpur region in Jharkhand to Prayagraj in Uttar Pradesh and then to Almora in the hills of Uttarakhand. Out of the window you see rocky uplands, then flat farmland, then steep forested hills. The land changes, and so does the way people live. In this chapter we study these landforms and their influence on life.'),
 [('The three main landforms',['A landform is a natural feature of the Earth\'s surface. Broadly there are three kinds: mountains, plateaus and plains.','Seen from a plane, or from a satellite, the differences are clear. Mountains rise high, plateaus are high and flat on top, and plains are wide flat lands where rivers flow.']),
  ('Mountains',['Mountains are landforms much higher than the land around them. At very great heights it is cold enough for snow to fall and stay, so the peaks are snow-capped. At lower heights the snow melts every summer and feeds rivers.','Mount Everest in the Himalayas is the highest peak in the world. Tibetans call it Chomolungma, the Mother Goddess of the World. Mount Aconcagua in South America is the highest peak of the Andes, and Anamudi in Kerala is the highest in south India.','Mountain slopes are often covered with montane forests of pine, fir, spruce and deodar. Steep slopes and cold weather make regular farming possible only in some valleys, so herding is preferred in many mountain regions.','Tourism is an important income for mountain people, and for many centuries people have travelled to the mountains on pilgrimages. Mountains can also bring dangers such as landslides, which are sudden collapses of rock or earth from a slope. Arunima Sinha, who lost a leg in an accident, became the first Indian woman to climb Mount Everest with a prosthetic leg, showing human courage.']),
  ('Plateaus',['A plateau is a large area of high land with a flat top and steep sides. The Tibetan Plateau is the highest and largest in the world and the Deccan Plateau covers much of peninsular India.','Plateaus are called storehouses of minerals. The Chhota Nagpur Plateau has huge reserves of iron, coal and manganese. Lava plateaus, formed by volcanic activity, have rich black soil.','Rivers that flow over a plateau tumble over its edge as waterfalls. The Nohkalikai Falls in Meghalaya drop 340 metres from the Cherrapunji Plateau.']),
  ('Plains',['Plains are large flat or gently sloping lands. Many plains are formed by rivers that carry rock particles, sand and silt, called sediments, from the mountains and spread them over the land. The fertile soil is called alluvium.','Plains are good for farming, roads and cities, so a large part of the world\'s people live on them. Crops such as rice, wheat, maize, barley and millets grow there, and canals and groundwater bring irrigation.','The Ganga plains of north India are among the most populated in the world. High population and pollution create problems for the river, so its care is a shared task.','Rivers are also waterways, and the Ganga has been used for transport for centuries. The meeting point of two or more rivers, called a confluence, such as at Prayagraj, is a place of festivals and pilgrimage.']),
  ('Deserts and resilience',['A desert is a very dry land with little rain. Some deserts are hot, like the Sahara in Africa and the Thar in India. Others are cold.','Communities of the Thar have rich traditions of folk songs and legends, and people there adapt with camels and careful use of water.','Each landform offers both challenges and opportunities. People respond with resilience, which is the ability to cope with and overcome difficulties.'])],
 [('A village lies on a river plain. Which landform and activities fit: farming, waterway transport, dense population?',[('Flat land with river sediments is a plain.','Look at the landform description.'),('Fertile soil allows farming of rice and wheat.','Plains are fertile.'),('River waterways and dense settlement go with plains, so the landform is a plain.','Use clues to decide.')]),
  ('Match: iron mines, rice fields, pilgrimage to a snowy shrine.',[('Iron mines belong to plateaus.','Plateaus are storehouses of minerals.'),('Rice fields belong to plains.','Fertile alluvium.'),('Pilgrimage to a snowy shrine belongs to mountains.','Mountains are held sacred.')])],
 ('Compare mountains, plateaus and plains and say how each affects people.',['Mountains are high with cold weather, give herding, tourism and pilgrimage.','Plateaus are flat-topped and rich in minerals.','Plains are flat and fertile so farming and cities grow there.'],['Thinking a plateau is the same as a plain.','Thinking all deserts are hot.']),
 ['Mountains, plateaus and plains are the main landforms.','Plateaus are rich in minerals; plains are fertile and crowded.','Mountains give rivers, pilgrimage and tourism but farming is hard.','People adapt to every landform with resilience.'],
 [('m','A high flat-topped land with steep sides is a','plateau','plain','valley','This describes a plateau.'),
  ('m','Rich iron and coal reserves are found in the','Chhota Nagpur Plateau','Ganga plains','Thar Desert','It is called a storehouse of minerals.'),
  ('m','Plains are mainly formed by','sediments deposited by rivers','volcanoes','glaciers only','Rivers spread sand and silt over the land.'),
  ('t','Farming is easy on steep mountain slopes.',False,'Steep slopes and cold make farming difficult.'),
  ('m','The highest plateau in the world is the','Tibetan Plateau','Deccan Plateau','Malwa Plateau','The Tibetan Plateau is the highest and largest.'),
  ('m','The highest peak in south India is','Anamudi','Mount Everest','Aconcagua','Anamudi is in Kerala.'),
  ('m','Lava plateaus often have','rich black soil','only sand','permanent ice','Volcanic material gives fertile black soil.'),
  ('m','Which crops are grown on fertile plains?','Rice, wheat and millets','Only apples','Only tea','Plains support staple food crops.'),
  ('t','All deserts are hot.',False,'Some deserts are cold.'),
  ('m','A river falling from the edge of a plateau forms a','waterfall','delta','lake','The drop makes a waterfall.')],
 keep=['plateau','plain','mountain'])
